WEBVTT

00:00:02.350 --> 00:00:03.850
Um...

00:00:04.170 --> 00:00:09.030
The cause of the stagnant water was found at its source in the ruins...

00:00:10.100 --> 00:00:11.820
Looks like you're having a hard time.

00:00:13.570 --> 00:00:16.070
I'm not very good at putting reports together.

00:00:16.560 --> 00:00:19.800
Logy-san, shouldn't you be working on yours?

00:00:19.800 --> 00:00:21.400
I turned mine in a long time ago.

00:00:21.400 --> 00:00:23.040
Huh? Since when?

00:00:24.190 --> 00:00:26.420
I wanted to look at yours before you turned it in.

00:00:26.750 --> 00:00:29.840
If you aren't good at it, that's all the more reason to work on it alone.

00:00:29.840 --> 00:00:31.670
Just like alchemy, it's important to practice.

00:00:32.080 --> 00:00:33.340
Yes.

00:00:35.500 --> 00:00:38.870
I'm thinking of reinforcing our equipment for later.

00:00:38.870 --> 00:00:41.220
Leave that to me.

00:00:41.220 --> 00:00:43.420
Yes, please.

00:00:50.330 --> 00:00:51.280
Absolutely not.

00:00:52.600 --> 00:00:56.040
There's no way I can approve a report with so many mistakes.

00:00:56.040 --> 00:00:58.030
Submit it again after you edit it.

00:00:58.520 --> 00:01:01.240
B-But Marion's out!

00:01:01.860 --> 00:01:03.780
It's up to you to work it out.

00:01:07.310 --> 00:01:09.960
I guess there's someone who's even worse off.

00:02:49.980 --> 00:02:53.160
Feel free to use it.

00:02:54.690 --> 00:02:57.230
It looks well made!

00:02:57.230 --> 00:03:00.410
I'm sure it'll be very comfy after we clean it up a little.

00:03:00.700 --> 00:03:03.340
Is it really okay for us to borrow it?

00:03:03.340 --> 00:03:08.480
Yes, we only use this Apple House during the harvest.

00:03:08.480 --> 00:03:11.920
The entire town's overjoyed that an apothecary such as yourself is here.

00:03:11.920 --> 00:03:14.040
Doctors are hard to come by here.

00:03:14.040 --> 00:03:16.800
Please let me know if you need anything.

00:03:17.130 --> 00:03:18.310
Really?

00:03:18.310 --> 00:03:19.550
Then...!

00:03:19.550 --> 00:03:21.680
No, we're fine!

00:03:22.920 --> 00:03:24.350
My oh my.

00:03:33.130 --> 00:03:35.860
Let's make this our base of operations for the time being.

00:03:35.860 --> 00:03:37.670
You could've stayed here too, Wilbell-san.

00:03:37.670 --> 00:03:39.370
Don't you worry.

00:03:39.370 --> 00:03:41.610
I go where the wind blows,

00:03:42.170 --> 00:03:45.310
and live freely as a wanderer!

00:03:45.310 --> 00:03:48.120
So it really is the two of you.

00:03:48.440 --> 00:03:49.580
Marion-san.

00:03:49.880 --> 00:03:53.700
Well, I guessed as much when I saw Linca.

00:03:53.700 --> 00:03:56.750
So what's an elite from Central City like you doing in a rural area like this?

00:03:57.300 --> 00:03:58.850
A lot has happened.

00:03:58.850 --> 00:04:01.130
Right now, I'm the R&D chief here.

00:04:02.480 --> 00:04:04.540
So that makes you their boss.

00:04:04.540 --> 00:04:05.620
That's right.

00:04:05.620 --> 00:04:09.390
Marion-san, have you heard anything about my sister?

00:04:09.390 --> 00:04:10.500
Anything at all?

00:04:10.500 --> 00:04:12.020
Nio-chan.

00:04:13.240 --> 00:04:15.980
Even if I did, I couldn't tell you.

00:04:15.980 --> 00:04:17.610
Think about it from my perspective.

00:04:18.270 --> 00:04:21.240
You're as blockheaded as ever.

00:04:21.240 --> 00:04:25.630
Normally I would need to report this to the Central City,

00:04:25.630 --> 00:04:30.540
but seeing that you helped those two out, I'll turn a blind eye.

00:04:30.540 --> 00:04:32.070
Marion-san.

00:04:33.210 --> 00:04:36.080
However, don't cause trouble in town.

00:04:36.080 --> 00:04:37.170
Wilbell, that goes double for you!

00:04:38.320 --> 00:04:39.920
Okay, I get it!

00:04:39.920 --> 00:04:41.000
Later.

00:04:44.810 --> 00:04:47.850
I'm also searching for her myself.

00:04:57.290 --> 00:04:59.420
Nio-san! Wilbell-san!

00:04:59.420 --> 00:05:01.570
Was the chief here just now?

00:05:01.570 --> 00:05:03.420
Yeah, we know each other.

00:05:03.420 --> 00:05:05.700
We met before.

00:05:05.700 --> 00:05:07.940
Eh? Really?

00:05:07.940 --> 00:05:10.620
That's right. We didn't tell you?

00:05:10.620 --> 00:05:13.230
Of course, we know that idiot swordsgirl too.

00:05:13.230 --> 00:05:14.580
You know Linca-san too?

00:05:14.860 --> 00:05:16.330
That's rude.

00:05:18.390 --> 00:05:20.890
Oh, that's right, I heard this from Clone.

00:05:20.890 --> 00:05:22.550
Nio-san, you're going to live here, right?

00:05:22.770 --> 00:05:24.760
Yeah, for now.

00:05:24.760 --> 00:05:25.930
She's opening an apothecary.

00:05:27.380 --> 00:05:30.700
But is a storage room really going to work for you?

00:05:32.260 --> 00:05:33.600
Let's remodel the place!

00:05:45.540 --> 00:05:49.030
Once you start, you can really get into it.

00:05:51.270 --> 00:05:52.800
Is here okay?

00:05:52.800 --> 00:05:53.910
Yes.

00:05:54.980 --> 00:05:56.000
Barrel!

00:05:58.460 --> 00:06:00.820
Hey, what is this?

00:06:01.880 --> 00:06:04.050
Oh, you felt that?

00:06:04.960 --> 00:06:07.030
Of course.

00:06:07.030 --> 00:06:08.230
What is it?

00:06:08.230 --> 00:06:09.220
How does it work?

00:06:10.040 --> 00:06:11.600
I've been wondering the same thing.

00:06:11.950 --> 00:06:14.370
It's just an accessory!

00:06:14.370 --> 00:06:16.800
Even though you can move and feel it?

00:06:17.840 --> 00:06:19.520
Was it made with alchemy?

00:06:19.770 --> 00:06:21.220
I knew you'd know!

00:06:21.220 --> 00:06:25.400
That's right, my mother made it for me when I was a kid.

00:06:25.640 --> 00:06:27.650
Is your mother an alchemist too?

00:06:27.920 --> 00:06:29.120
Yes.

00:06:29.120 --> 00:06:31.600
Or rather, she was.

00:06:31.600 --> 00:06:34.620
She died during an epidemic when I was still young.

00:06:35.660 --> 00:06:36.870
I-I'm sorry.

00:06:37.220 --> 00:06:38.300
Don't worry.

00:06:38.300 --> 00:06:40.880
To be honest, I don't remember much about her.

00:06:41.670 --> 00:06:45.250
It's strange that you remember the alchemy she taught you.

00:06:45.760 --> 00:06:47.460
That's true.

00:06:48.400 --> 00:06:51.980
Escha, I thought you were quite an easygoing and carefree person,

00:06:51.980 --> 00:06:53.840
but I didn't realise you had such a tough past.

00:06:53.840 --> 00:06:55.560
Not at all!

00:06:55.880 --> 00:06:56.660
Huh?

00:06:56.660 --> 00:06:59.730
Did you just say something bad about me without me noticing?

00:07:04.680 --> 00:07:07.860
Well, this turned out quite well with just a bit of work.

00:07:07.860 --> 00:07:10.280
I don't remember you doing very much.

00:07:11.080 --> 00:07:13.160
Next, we need to get ourselves some furniture.

00:07:13.910 --> 00:07:15.320
What do you need?

00:07:15.320 --> 00:07:18.290
I guess a bed, a table, and a chair?

00:07:18.630 --> 00:07:20.550
You need a good sense of aesthetics to choose the right decorations,

00:07:20.550 --> 00:07:22.330
so Nio and I will take care of that.

00:07:22.330 --> 00:07:23.630
You two can get the furniture.

00:07:23.860 --> 00:07:25.070
Yes!

00:07:25.070 --> 00:07:26.720
Huh? Aesthetic sense?

00:07:26.720 --> 00:07:29.710
Is a folding table good enough?

00:07:29.710 --> 00:07:30.590
Actually, if possible...

00:07:31.950 --> 00:07:34.550
A big table...

00:07:34.830 --> 00:07:37.130
Does she need such a big table for herself?

00:07:37.130 --> 00:07:39.560
She must need it for synthesising medicine.

00:07:40.330 --> 00:07:42.520
Where can we buy furniture?

00:07:44.170 --> 00:07:45.380
Good question...

00:07:45.380 --> 00:07:47.980
Why, hello, you alchemists over there.

00:07:48.640 --> 00:07:52.030
And the suspicious-looking lady.

00:07:52.030 --> 00:07:53.910
Oh, Katla-chan. Hello.

00:07:54.780 --> 00:07:56.370
Who are you calling suspicious?

00:07:57.250 --> 00:07:59.440
Oh, my mistake.

00:07:59.440 --> 00:08:03.340
I meant the suspicious-looking beauty.

00:08:03.340 --> 00:08:04.540
That works.

00:08:04.540 --> 00:08:06.000
It does?

00:08:06.240 --> 00:08:07.850
Oh yeah, Katla-chan.

00:08:07.850 --> 00:08:08.530
Yes?

00:08:08.530 --> 00:08:11.010
Do you sell furniture here?

00:08:11.010 --> 00:08:11.900
Come on.

00:08:11.900 --> 00:08:14.470
No matter how you look at it, she only has sundries.

00:08:14.470 --> 00:08:16.980
Of course I do!

00:08:16.980 --> 00:08:20.180
As long as you need it, I can get it for you!

00:08:22.260 --> 00:08:24.020
Really?!

00:08:24.020 --> 00:08:25.400
Hold it, Escha.

00:08:25.400 --> 00:08:27.330
She's a crafty girl.

00:08:27.330 --> 00:08:29.860
No doubt she'll charge you a large commission.

00:08:30.540 --> 00:08:33.220
Sorry, I'm going to have to...

00:08:33.220 --> 00:08:34.540
A tail!

00:08:35.190 --> 00:08:36.830
I want a tail like this too!

00:08:36.830 --> 00:08:37.870
You can't.

00:08:37.870 --> 00:08:39.330
That's her's.

00:08:39.330 --> 00:08:40.970
I really want one!

00:08:40.970 --> 00:08:42.990
Enough already.

00:08:42.990 --> 00:08:44.480
I want one!

00:08:44.480 --> 00:08:45.460
We're leaving.

00:08:45.460 --> 00:08:46.900
Sorry about this.

00:08:46.900 --> 00:08:47.790
I want one!

00:08:48.960 --> 00:08:51.280
I knew that tail would attract attention.

00:08:51.280 --> 00:08:52.520
Especially kids.

00:08:52.520 --> 00:08:54.930
I-Is that so?

00:08:56.400 --> 00:09:00.810
Alchemist lady, would you please sell your tail to me?

00:09:01.540 --> 00:09:03.040
I-I won't!

00:09:03.040 --> 00:09:04.890
How much do you want for it?

00:09:04.890 --> 00:09:07.150
I'll pay a lot for it!

00:09:07.370 --> 00:09:09.400
It's not about money.

00:09:09.620 --> 00:09:10.940
Hey, you.

00:09:10.940 --> 00:09:12.900
How much is a lot?

00:09:14.950 --> 00:09:16.240
I think you should sell it!

00:09:17.160 --> 00:09:18.370
Wilbell-san?

00:09:18.370 --> 00:09:20.580
Why are you following their lead?

00:09:20.580 --> 00:09:21.920
I'm not selling it!

00:09:21.920 --> 00:09:24.330
This is something precious my mother left behind!

00:09:26.100 --> 00:09:27.140
Is that so?

00:09:27.140 --> 00:09:29.590
I won't force you if it has sentimental value.

00:09:30.500 --> 00:09:32.840
I can understand. Your mother passed away, after all.

00:09:33.380 --> 00:09:34.710
I'm sorry.

00:09:34.710 --> 00:09:36.960
If this was made with alchemy,

00:09:36.960 --> 00:09:39.350
couldn't we make another?

00:09:40.350 --> 00:09:42.260
Theoretically, anyway.

00:09:43.660 --> 00:09:45.220
That's it!

00:09:47.340 --> 00:09:48.280
Listen up!

00:09:48.280 --> 00:09:51.730
Colseit's main source of income is from its specialities,

00:09:51.730 --> 00:09:53.030
and that means selling apples!

00:09:53.540 --> 00:09:56.900
But that only happens once a year during the harvest.

00:09:56.900 --> 00:10:01.240
Outside of that, we get by with occasional trading.

00:10:01.240 --> 00:10:03.830
It's no surprise our economy is poor.

00:10:04.760 --> 00:10:05.710
However!

00:10:05.710 --> 00:10:12.050
If we mass produce this novel accessory and sell it to Central City,

00:10:12.050 --> 00:10:17.210
it will likely cause a huge boom, and our town's economy will thrive!

00:10:17.210 --> 00:10:21.680
It will be the end of all our financial problems!

00:10:23.380 --> 00:10:25.340
I don't think it'll go that well.

00:10:25.340 --> 00:10:27.610
Well, it's not impossible.

00:10:27.610 --> 00:10:29.400
N-Not you too, Logy-san!

00:10:29.400 --> 00:10:30.150
Sorry.

00:10:30.500 --> 00:10:34.020
Alchemy isn't something you use to get rich!

00:10:34.020 --> 00:10:36.690
It exists only to make people happy!

00:10:36.690 --> 00:10:39.410
You're quite mistaken, this would make people plenty happy.

00:10:39.410 --> 00:10:40.910
I think so too!

00:10:40.910 --> 00:10:43.320
Anyway, I'm going to buy a table!

00:10:43.320 --> 00:10:44.980
Let's go, Logy-san.

00:10:44.980 --> 00:10:46.370
Yeah.

00:11:12.080 --> 00:11:13.330
What a nice sound.

00:11:13.330 --> 00:11:14.400
I see.

00:11:14.400 --> 00:11:16.570
We should be able to get one here.

00:11:16.570 --> 00:11:18.070
Isn't it Escha?

00:11:19.570 --> 00:11:21.880
Huh? Onii-chan?

00:11:21.880 --> 00:11:24.070
Hey, Escha-chan.

00:11:24.670 --> 00:11:26.010
Good afternoon.

00:11:26.010 --> 00:11:26.830
What's going on?

00:11:27.230 --> 00:11:30.590
We are thinking of replacing a few wooden floor planks at the port.

00:11:30.590 --> 00:11:32.040
What about you?

00:11:32.040 --> 00:11:33.590
Apple barrels?

00:11:33.590 --> 00:11:34.580
Not today.

00:11:34.580 --> 00:11:36.140
We're here for furniture.

00:11:36.140 --> 00:11:36.670
Furniture?

00:11:37.240 --> 00:11:40.140
A bed, a table, and a chair.

00:11:40.140 --> 00:11:41.890
What's that, Escha-chan?

00:11:41.890 --> 00:11:44.550
You letting that guy live with you?

00:11:44.840 --> 00:11:46.380
You're mistaken.

00:11:46.380 --> 00:11:48.440
We're just helping someone else.

00:11:48.440 --> 00:11:49.680
Right.

00:11:49.680 --> 00:11:50.770
Don't surprise me.

00:11:51.150 --> 00:11:53.270
Not you too, Brother.

00:11:55.440 --> 00:11:57.020
So what are you looking for?

00:11:57.990 --> 00:11:59.560
Well, let's see...

00:11:59.560 --> 00:12:01.490
Wouldn't that do?

00:12:03.490 --> 00:12:05.340
That doesn't work, Logy-san.

00:12:05.340 --> 00:12:08.340
Think about it from Nio-san's point of view.

00:12:08.340 --> 00:12:10.110
Is that so?

00:12:10.110 --> 00:12:12.340
I guess I don't understand.

00:12:12.340 --> 00:12:13.780
You can custom order one too.

00:12:13.780 --> 00:12:15.920
Whatever it is you need, we can make it for you.

00:12:15.920 --> 00:12:16.590
Anything?

00:12:17.020 --> 00:12:18.010
Of course.

00:12:18.010 --> 00:12:19.210
We <i>are</i> artisans.

00:12:19.630 --> 00:12:25.550
Even though we can't use alchemy,
we have our age old tools and these arms!

00:12:25.550 --> 00:12:27.810
I'll make you anything.

00:12:27.810 --> 00:12:29.640
Even a drawing of what you envision will do.

00:12:32.960 --> 00:12:34.480
Like this?

00:12:40.870 --> 00:12:42.140
Later.

00:12:42.140 --> 00:12:43.490
See you!

00:12:44.480 --> 00:12:46.820
I'm impressed they'll finish it in three days.

00:12:47.140 --> 00:12:48.420
Yeah.

00:12:48.420 --> 00:12:51.920
It reminds me that artisans and alchemists are no different.

00:12:51.920 --> 00:12:55.040
They both learn and perfect their trade.

00:12:58.490 --> 00:13:01.020
Um, Logy-san.

00:13:01.020 --> 00:13:01.840
What's the matter?

00:13:02.260 --> 00:13:04.090
I want to try...

00:13:05.420 --> 00:13:07.220
...synthesizing a tail.

00:13:08.570 --> 00:13:10.510
You'd do that for me?!

00:13:10.920 --> 00:13:13.930
Yeah, I am not too confident, but I'll try.

00:13:13.930 --> 00:13:15.520
Please!

00:13:15.910 --> 00:13:18.270
Yay! Yay!

00:13:22.420 --> 00:13:25.300
Why do you want to try making it all of a sudden?

00:13:25.300 --> 00:13:32.300
My sick mother made me this tail so that I wouldn't be lonely.

00:13:33.340 --> 00:13:36.980
I helped out when she made it.

00:13:37.960 --> 00:13:42.300
I learned the basics of alchemy from my mother.

00:13:42.300 --> 00:13:44.090
Yeah, you told me.

00:13:44.840 --> 00:13:52.860
Didn't you say that it's strange I don't remember anything about my mother but still remember alchemy?

00:13:52.860 --> 00:13:57.800
It's pretty hard to forget a skill once you get the hang of it.

00:14:03.080 --> 00:14:09.280
I thought I might be able to remember more about my mother if I make this tail once more.

00:14:10.160 --> 00:14:11.560
It's no good.

00:14:11.560 --> 00:14:12.990
Not a single one of these books mention it!

00:14:13.320 --> 00:14:16.220
I've never heard of a moving tail,

00:14:16.220 --> 00:14:18.940
let alone one that links with your senses.

00:14:18.940 --> 00:14:19.780
That's it!

00:14:19.780 --> 00:14:21.420
Maybe Clone knows something about it!

00:14:22.320 --> 00:14:23.370
My oh my.

00:14:23.370 --> 00:14:25.340
The tail's recipe, is it?

00:14:25.700 --> 00:14:27.990
Yeah, did she leave it behind?

00:14:27.990 --> 00:14:32.680
Miria wasn't someone who would write her recipes down.

00:14:33.260 --> 00:14:35.230
She was a rather careless person, after all.

00:14:35.230 --> 00:14:35.970
I guess.

00:14:36.600 --> 00:14:40.520
Still, that doesn't necessarily mean no information.

00:14:44.210 --> 00:14:46.190
This is all of the data.

00:14:47.630 --> 00:14:48.770
Thanks.

00:14:48.770 --> 00:14:50.610
I'll take a look.

00:14:51.550 --> 00:14:53.600
It's not here.

00:14:53.600 --> 00:14:56.500
There's not much here on alchemy.

00:14:56.940 --> 00:14:58.590
That's true.

00:15:00.410 --> 00:15:03.000
Huh? This picture book...

00:15:04.010 --> 00:15:06.590
The Adventures of the Hummingbird Princess?

00:15:06.590 --> 00:15:07.550
That's right.

00:15:07.550 --> 00:15:10.300
I used to have Clone read this to me all the time when I was little.

00:15:10.710 --> 00:15:12.590
This brings back memories.

00:15:27.070 --> 00:15:30.930
These things happen when people can't find what they need.

00:15:31.480 --> 00:15:35.170
I... remembered.

00:15:36.080 --> 00:15:37.390
That's right!

00:15:37.390 --> 00:15:38.450
It was when...

00:15:42.600 --> 00:15:45.170
I gathered the ingredients to the best of my memory.

00:15:45.170 --> 00:15:47.220
It looks like you could cook something with those.

00:15:47.220 --> 00:15:49.130
Anyway, let's give it a try.

00:16:49.960 --> 00:16:50.980
So?

00:16:51.320 --> 00:16:53.530
You managed to make it, but it doesn't move?

00:16:53.770 --> 00:16:56.720
It's just an accessory with a similar appearance.

00:16:56.720 --> 00:16:58.020
I'm sorry.

00:16:58.020 --> 00:17:01.500
I don't know if it's just because I'm not skilled enough or if I'm still missing something.

00:17:01.500 --> 00:17:03.750
It still turned out pretty well, if you ask me.

00:17:04.020 --> 00:17:07.320
My dreams of founding the Katla Company...!

00:17:07.320 --> 00:17:08.210
What a shame...

00:17:08.210 --> 00:17:11.000
I knew you were scheming something.

00:17:11.440 --> 00:17:14.220
If something that's supposed to move isn't moving,

00:17:15.800 --> 00:17:17.800
we'll just have to make it move!

00:17:19.590 --> 00:17:22.210
O Spirits that govern items!

00:17:31.640 --> 00:17:33.170
Logy-san, there!

00:17:33.170 --> 00:17:34.070
Katla, hurry!

00:17:34.070 --> 00:17:35.810
Even if you say so...!

00:17:35.810 --> 00:17:36.660
What's the fuss?

00:17:37.040 --> 00:17:38.140
Don't let it run away!

00:17:39.630 --> 00:17:40.640
What's that?!

00:17:40.640 --> 00:17:41.830
Stand back, Marion!

00:17:42.980 --> 00:17:43.790
Linca-san!

00:17:47.890 --> 00:17:49.600
T-This thing...!

00:17:55.630 --> 00:17:58.660
Wilbell-san, what did you do?

00:17:58.660 --> 00:17:59.600
I don't know!

00:18:11.060 --> 00:18:12.020
Marion-san!

00:18:16.390 --> 00:18:17.420
Chief...

00:18:17.420 --> 00:18:18.710
Oh no!

00:18:18.710 --> 00:18:21.070
Maybe some animal deity possessed it.

00:18:21.350 --> 00:18:23.550
D-Do something!

00:18:23.550 --> 00:18:24.450
Escha!

00:18:31.590 --> 00:18:33.170
Not Wilbell-san too!

00:18:35.090 --> 00:18:37.340
Although different, this might earn some big bucks!

00:18:38.860 --> 00:18:39.640
Watch out!

00:18:45.620 --> 00:18:47.590
My oh my, everyone's here.

00:18:47.590 --> 00:18:48.350
Stay away!

00:18:48.350 --> 00:18:49.640
Run!

00:18:54.010 --> 00:18:54.980
My oh my.

00:19:01.790 --> 00:19:03.240
I caught it!

00:19:03.240 --> 00:19:04.390
Good work!

00:19:05.890 --> 00:19:07.930
Logy-san!

00:19:07.930 --> 00:19:09.640
Don't let go of it.

00:19:09.640 --> 00:19:12.310
Is there anything we can put it in?

00:19:12.800 --> 00:19:15.490
And here I was wondering why no one's at the branch.

00:19:17.170 --> 00:19:18.380
What are you doing?

00:19:19.110 --> 00:19:20.930
I can't hold on anymore...

00:19:21.480 --> 00:19:22.680
Solle-san, watch out!

00:19:29.150 --> 00:19:31.310
Escha-kun, Logy.

00:19:32.400 --> 00:19:34.360
Why's everyone here?

00:19:34.360 --> 00:19:36.730
Seems quite lively out here.

00:19:36.730 --> 00:19:38.150
Branch Manager!

00:19:38.150 --> 00:19:39.510
You can't come here now!

00:19:39.510 --> 00:19:40.580
Get away!

00:19:41.640 --> 00:19:43.120
Pardon me?

00:19:44.190 --> 00:19:46.180
What? N-Not there!

00:19:52.400 --> 00:19:54.420
This is terrible.

00:20:00.780 --> 00:20:05.510
I told you not to cause trouble!

00:20:05.510 --> 00:20:09.430
Geez, you people!

00:20:06.770 --> 00:20:09.430
In the end, I'm getting scolded too.

00:20:14.080 --> 00:20:16.970
After the report, I have to write a reflection essay.

00:20:16.970 --> 00:20:19.650
Well, isn't it okay since everyone just laughed it off and forgave you?

00:20:20.150 --> 00:20:22.170
That's true, but...

00:20:22.170 --> 00:20:28.020
The tail stopped moving after Wilbell-san's magic wore off.

00:20:30.590 --> 00:20:33.670
I guess that means I still have a long way to go until I'm as skilled as my mother.

00:20:34.340 --> 00:20:37.130
In the end, just what were we missing?

00:20:37.550 --> 00:20:40.630
Perhaps it's a lack of feelings.

00:20:42.660 --> 00:20:48.610
Like a desire to ensure your daughter doesn't feel lonely even though you're sick and can't take care of her.

00:20:54.360 --> 00:20:55.480
Right!

00:21:10.990 --> 00:21:12.910
I hope you'll like this.

00:21:13.350 --> 00:21:15.170
Let's dig in!

00:21:18.780 --> 00:21:19.800
It's delicious!

00:21:21.480 --> 00:21:24.800
Well, they don't taste as good as the sweets I make.

00:21:25.210 --> 00:21:27.340
You make sweets, Wilbell-san?

00:21:27.830 --> 00:21:29.160
Of course.

00:21:29.160 --> 00:21:32.610
Sweets that mages make are naturally delicious.

00:21:33.580 --> 00:21:35.730
I didn't know.

00:21:35.730 --> 00:21:37.600
Wait, you really didn't know?

00:21:40.380 --> 00:21:43.490
So this is why you needed a big table.

00:21:44.250 --> 00:21:46.530
Thanks, both of you.

00:21:46.530 --> 00:21:48.490
Thank you for such a wonderful table.

00:21:48.940 --> 00:21:51.880
Could you make me some sweets next time?

00:21:51.880 --> 00:21:54.000
I can't do it for free.

00:21:55.640 --> 00:21:58.260
It's okay, right?
